{
  "$schema": "model-router example — copy to model-router.json and edit; never commit real keys",
  "comment": "Alpha 2: 50+ models, ranked by task strength — NOT by fame. rank = strength tier for THAT task (1 = strongest in this config for this task, 3 = weakest fallback), judged on public benchmark results and task capability. A lesser-known model can outrank a famous one for a specific task. The router tries entries in order and falls back on failure or limit (see scripts/route-model.js). Paid entries are used ONLY if you list them yourself. Free limits are real and pooled, not limitless: OpenRouter :free is 20 req/min, 50/day, 1000/day after $10 lifetime purchases; Groq free is per-model (main chat models 30 req/min, 1000/day, 8K tok/min, 200K tok/day); Gemini and SambaNova free tiers have their own per-model caps (check their consoles); Ollama local has no meter, limited by your hardware. Free-model rosters change often — verify in each provider console before relying on an entry. See docs/FREE-MODELS.md and docs/MODEL-ROUTER.md.",
